## 4. Schema Deltas (canonical shapes)

These are contract schemas, not code. Field types use JSON Schema vocab.

### 4.1 Envelope schema delta
- `data` MUST be present on success; MUST be `null` on error.
- `error.code` MUST match `^ERR_[A-Z]+(?:_[A-Z0-9]+)+$`.
- `meta.audit_id` MUST be present for any 2xx response on a mutating route.
- `meta.etag` MUST be present on any resource that supports `If-Match`.

### 4.2 Resource: Monitor
```jsonc
{
  "monitor_id":     "string",
  "name":           "string",
  "owner":          "string",
  "script_path":    "string",
  "status":         "active | broken | unused | duplicate | unknown",
  "last_run":       "RFC3339 | null",
  "last_success":   "RFC3339 | null",
  "last_failure":   "RFC3339 | null",
  "metrics_emitted":["string"],
  "redis_keys":     ["string"],
  "logs_watched":   ["string"],
  "processes":      ["string"],
  "alerts_24h":     "integer >= 0",
  "evidence_refs":  [ { "type": "code|redis|log|db|cmd|config", "pointer": "string" } ]
}
```
Delta vs prior drafts: `status` enum is closed; `evidence_refs[]` mandatory (Evidence Integrity Rule); no free-form "notes" field.

### 4.3 Resource: SignalExplanation
```jsonc
{
  "signal_id":         "string",
  "symbol":            "string",
  "generated_at":      "RFC3339",
  "input_data_ref":    "string",                // pointer to immutable input snapshot
  "feature_snapshot":  { "<feature>": "number|string|null" },
  "feature_freshness": { "<feature>": "RFC3339" },
  "raw_model_output":  { /* opaque */ },
  "confidence":        "number 0..1",
  "calibration":       { "method": "string", "params": { } },
  "model_version":     "string",
  "checkpoint_id":     "string",
  "orchestrator_reason":"string",
  "risk_gateway":      {
    "decision":        "allow | block",
    "reasons":         ["string"],
    "policy_version":  "string"
  },
  "config_version":    "string",
  "evidence_refs":     [ { "type": "...", "pointer": "string" } ],
  "missing_evidence":  ["string"]
}
```
Delta: `risk_gateway` is its own object (was previously a string); `missing_evidence[]` mandatory.

