- [ ] `openapi.v2.yaml` exists and validates against the matrix in §3.
- [ ] Every endpoint in §3 has: method, path, role, scopes[], idempotency flag, dangerous flag, request schema ref, response schema ref, error code list.
- [ ] Standard envelope (§2.4) is the only response shape; no naked bodies.
- [ ] Error code registry (§4.6) exists as a closed enum referenced by openapi.
- [ ] Idempotency middleware contract documented and referenced by every POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE in §3.
- [ ] RBAC scope set (§2.7) documented; every endpoint declares required scopes.
- [ ] Dangerous-action gate (§6) lists every route that touches live, leverage, margin, kill switch, or promotion to live; each requires `X-Actor-Confirm` + MFA + `live_authority`.
- [ ] Audit propagation rule (§2.10) covered — every mutating 2xx returns `meta.audit_id`.
- [ ] Streaming contract (§7) covered — envelope, heartbeats, scope re-check.
- [ ] Codex re-review references this file by path and signs off on tasks 002/004 blocker.

