## 9. Core Payload Schemas (deltas vs. scaffold)

Below are the contract-level schemas the scaffold must adopt. They replace any `Dict[str, Any]` placeholders currently in the FastAPI scaffold and the SPA's `apiClient`.

```python
# common.py
class Envelope(BaseModel, Generic[T]):
    ok: Literal[True]
    request_id: str
    issued_at: datetime
    schema_version: Literal["v2.1"]
    data: T
    warnings: list[Warning] = []
    meta: Meta | None = None

class Warning(BaseModel):
    code: WarningCode
    message: str
    details: dict[str, Any] = {}

class ErrorEnvelope(BaseModel):
    ok: Literal[False]
    request_id: str
    issued_at: datetime
    schema_version: Literal["v2.1"]
    error: ErrorObject

class ErrorObject(BaseModel):
    code: ErrorCode
    http_status: int
    message: str
    details: dict[str, Any] = {}
    retryable: bool
    retry_after_ms: int | None
    evidence: EvidenceRef

class EvidenceRef(BaseModel):
    audit_ledger_id: str | None
    redis_key: str | None
    log_pointer: str | None
```

```python
# mission_control.py
class MissionControlSummary(BaseModel):
    mode: Literal["paper", "replay", "read_only"]
    live_blocked: Literal[True]              # constant in V2
    legacy_adapter: AdapterStatus
    redis: DependencyStatus
    db: DependencyStatus
    monitors: MonitorsSummary
    trainer: TrainerSummary
    risk_gateway: RiskGatewaySummary
    last_signal: SignalSummary | None
    last_execution: ExecutionSummary | None
    coverage: CoverageSummary
    build: BuildSummary
```

```python
# signal_explainability.py
class SignalExplainability(BaseModel):
    signal_id: str
    symbol: str
    issued_at: datetime
    model_version: str
    checkpoint_id: str
    config_version_id: str
    feature_snapshot: FeatureSnapshotRef         # id + freshness_ms + missing[]
    raw_model_output: RawModelOutput             # logits/probas + shape
    confidence: ConfidenceBreakdown              # calibrated + raw + buckets
    orchestrator_reason: OrchestratorReason
    risk_gateway_reason: RiskDecision            # see §6
    redis_refs: list[RedisRef]
    db_refs: list[DbRef]
    log_refs: list[LogRef]
    missing_evidence: list[MissingEvidence]      # MUST be empty for "verified"
```

```python
# paper_order.py
class PaperOrderRequest(BaseModel):
    symbol: str
    side: Literal["buy", "sell"]
    quantity: Decimal                            # string in JSON
    order_type: Literal["market", "limit"]
    limit_price: Decimal | None
    time_in_force: Literal["GTC", "IOC", "FOK"] = "GTC"
    strategy_id: str
    config_version_id: str
    feature_snapshot_id: str | None
    prediction_id: str | None
    client_note: str | None

class PaperOrderAck(BaseModel):
    order_id: str
    state: Literal["accepted", "filled", "partially_filled", "rejected", "cancelled"]
    risk_decision: RiskDecision                  # always present
    fills: list[Fill] = []
    audit_ledger_id: str
```

```python
# config_admin.py
class ConfigDocument(BaseModel):
    namespace: str
    version_id: str                              # monotonic ULID
    if_match: str | None                         # required on PUT
    payload: dict[str, Any]                      # validated by namespace schema
    schema_id: str                               # ref to JSON Schema doc
    authored_by: ActorRef
    authored_at: datetime
    paper_safe: bool                             # false ⇒ §8.1 path
```

```python
# audit_ledger.py
class AuditRow(BaseModel):
    audit_ledger_id: str
    request_id: str
    actor: ActorRef
    route: str
    intent: str
    proposal: RiskProposal | None
    decision: RiskDecision | None
    result: dict[str, Any] | None
    evidence: EvidenceRef
    created_at: datetime
```

TypeScript mirrors are generated from these via `openapi-typescript` and committed under `v2/web/src/generated/api/`. The SPA's `apiClient` is forbidden from inlining any of these shapes.

